# Copy to .env.local for local dev (with `supabase start` running, these
# match its printed output) or fill in from your Supabase project settings.

NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=

# Server-only. NEVER prefix this with NEXT_PUBLIC_, never import it from
# client code — it bypasses RLS entirely. Used by src/lib/supabase/admin.ts
# (issue #24, the "Invite (opnieuw) versturen"-knop in Ledenbeheer) for
# supabase.auth.admin.inviteUserByEmail() — the only file allowed to read
# this var, see ADR 0006. Required as soon as that feature is used; leaving
# it unset means the invite action fails with "unknown", not a silent no-op.
# SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY=

# Server-only — the shared bar-tablet's Supabase Auth account. src/middleware.ts
# signs in as this account (server-side, via cookies) when a bar-shell request
# has no session yet. See docs/ARCHITECTURE.md → "Shared bar-tablet session
# mechanism" and issue #32. Provisioning this account in Supabase itself is a
# manual ops step (Studio/CLI), not something the app does.
# SUPABASE_DEVICE_EMAIL=
# SUPABASE_DEVICE_PASSWORD=

# Server-only. NEVER prefix this with NEXT_PUBLIC_. The koppelcode for the
# bar tablet (docs/features/tablet-koppelen.md, ADR 0011): src/middleware.ts
# only signs in as the device account above on a browser that was once
# gekoppeld on /koppel with this code, and it is the basis for the HMAC key
# of the `abas_tablet` cookie. Format: 26 characters base32 (A-Z, 2-7,
# 130 bit), groups with dashes are fine, case doesn't matter. Shorter, other
# characters, or unset → no koppeling and no device session anywhere (fails
# closed, one console.error). Locally: set it here and koppel your dev
# browser once via /koppel. Rotating it unkoppels every tablet at once.
# Generate one with:
#   node -e "const a='ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ234567';console.log(Array.from(require('crypto').randomBytes(26),b=>a[b&31]).join('').match(/.{1,5}/g).join('-'))"
# BAR_DEVICE_SECRET=

# Server-only — HTTP Basic Auth password for /design (the live design-bundle
# preview, see docs/ARCHITECTURE.md → Bronmateriaal). Only enforced in a
# production build (`next build && next start`, incl. Vercel); `next dev`
# stays ungated. Unset in production means /design 404s rather than being
# left open — set this before deploying if /design should be reachable there.
# DESIGN_PREVIEW_PASSWORD=
